{
  "id": "event-inbox-react-agent",
  "name": "event-inbox-react-agent",
  "description": "A resident ReAct agent (LLM + while loop, no Agent node) driven by an open event channel instead of any specific hub. It declares a named mailbox (events_mailbox var), parks durably on wait_event when idle, and drains its events_inbox run var with a seq cursor at EVERY cycle boundary - so events posted by anyone (humans, bridges, other agents) via the gateway emit_event command with durable:true interleave into the very next loop cycle, even mid-burst. A payload {kind: 'stop'} ends the resident. Agora, Telegram, cron, or a human are all just producers.",
  "interfaces": [],
  "nodes": [
